{
    "word": "quaternion",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                "word": "quaternion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9a68da56-aff4-4829-9456-bf581de8cac4",
                        "entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "quaternions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c18b91d-848d-37d5-a580-96e21f178454",
                        "entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A group or set of four people or things."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1d67ee7-2ea8-4907-9a6c-20ca53fa470d",
                                "sense_id": "1c18b91d-848d-37d5-a580-96e21f178454",
                                "text": "Then wer the dayes of unlevended breed, and when he had caught hym, he put him in preson, and delyvered hym to iiij. quaternions off soudiers to be kepte, entendynge after ester to brynge hym forth to the people."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "472ce7a2-5f8c-4b78-8aa3-f0a439f0ccdc",
                                "sense_id": "1c18b91d-848d-37d5-a580-96e21f178454",
                                "text": "This quaternion of revilers has traduced Origen, but not on the same grounds, one having found one cause of accusation against him, and another another; and thus each has demonstrated that what he has taken no objection to, he has fully accepted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53ae0c0c-0943-4308-868d-09b622686bff",
                                "sense_id": "1c18b91d-848d-37d5-a580-96e21f178454",
                                "text": "We saw above that the fourth quire consists of ten folios, two of which (folios 29 and 31) Richer added to a quaternion (folios 23 to 28, 30, 32). Most of the folios Richer added to his manuscript supplement, elaborate, or amend text that he had already composed in the codex."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf9d2b20-2b34-31b9-802c-f8db4f5a3267",
                        "entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A word of four syllables."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56b4269a-ee17-4eb3-973c-8a998c3f0fc2",
                                "sense_id": "cf9d2b20-2b34-31b9-802c-f8db4f5a3267",
                                "text": "In his general deportment he was pompous and important, affecting a species of florid elocution, which often became ridiculous from his misarranging the triads and quaternions with which he loaded his sentences."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1420314-62fd-3cae-85a0-41b775cd4393",
                        "entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of four-dimensional hypercomplex number consisting of a real part and three imaginary parts (real multiples of distinct, independent square roots of −1 denoted by i, j and k); commonly used in vector mathematics and as an alternative to matrix algebra in calculating the rotation of three-dimensional objects."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "21acf9da-d40d-41e7-af24-921d182bcfb8",
                                "sense_id": "d1420314-62fd-3cae-85a0-41b775cd4393",
                                "text": "The right-hand side of the quaternion equation requires scalar multiplication and quaternion addition."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5d8ad9d-46c8-46cd-9824-7dda3a8e905c",
                        "source_entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "source_sense_description": "a four-dimensional hypercomplex number",
                        "target_lang_word": "kvaternion",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "35d93385-e5f6-4474-b3c5-b4cadb335a83",
                        "source_entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "source_sense_description": "a four-dimensional hypercomplex number",
                        "target_lang_word": "quaternion",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quaternion",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "294a35d0-4ccd-3d6c-b101-3d48485535ae",
                                        "entry_id": "b0958181-0546-3266-96c1-29dd6d889759",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een hypercomplex getal bestaande uit vier reële delen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4864963-60fa-4214-b67d-ef186bbfdb28",
                                                "sense_id": "294a35d0-4ccd-3d6c-b101-3d48485535ae",
                                                "text": "Quaternionen zijn in 1843 door Sir William Hamilton ontdekt, maar pas aan het einde van de twintigste eeuw hebben zij toepassing gevonden."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "68fd93e7-282a-4252-8519-72102007a978",
                        "source_entry_id": "514a6ba7-4373-3bed-954c-6110bd874df8",
                        "source_sense_description": "a four-dimensional hypercomplex number",
                        "target_lang_word": "quaternion",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quaternion",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31b3e11b-0dce-3e4c-995e-3d8506565dfe",
                                        "entry_id": "e1f99d13-ec0d-3a5f-9972-3eb7db1bf87f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nombre découvert par le mathématicien irlandais William Rowan Hamilton, et qui s’écrit sous la forme a + bi + cj + dk avec i² = j² = k² = -1 et ij = -ji = k, jk = -kj = i et ki = -ik = j."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36debdcb-7d35-422d-8e2d-03f9d9d891b7",
                                                "sense_id": "31b3e11b-0dce-3e4c-995e-3d8506565dfe",
                                                "text": "L’ensemble des quaternions, noté ℍ, constitue une extension de l’ensemble des nombres complexes, extension similaire à celle qui avait conduit de l’ensemble des nombres réels ℝ à celui des nombres complexes ℂ, et qui conduira plus tard des quaternions aux octonions, 𝕆."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d8d353b-cd70-346d-87a7-ec6290ffc8b3",
                                        "entry_id": "e1f99d13-ec0d-3a5f-9972-3eb7db1bf87f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dans un codex ou un livre, cahier composé de quatre feuilles doubles (bifeuillets), soit 8 feuilles et 16 pages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Imprimerie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "581898f2-7add-4941-bc96-3ae0bc8fcc68",
                                                "sense_id": "9d8d353b-cd70-346d-87a7-ec6290ffc8b3",
                                                "text": "Le mot cahier vient du latin quaterni, quatre à la fois, qui a donné quaternio, quaternion en français, ou cahier de 4 feuillets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e67d66e6-d0b2-4a26-b765-13c17417cd08",
                                                "sense_id": "9d8d353b-cd70-346d-87a7-ec6290ffc8b3",
                                                "text": "Un quaternion de quatre bifeuillets. […] Le quaternion paraît avoir été le type de cahier le plus utilisé par les artisans occidentaux pour les manuscrits en parchemin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c48129a-36b2-44f4-82e0-ef1d79d2c657",
                                                "sense_id": "9d8d353b-cd70-346d-87a7-ec6290ffc8b3",
                                                "text": "Le nom du copiste à qui l’on doit cette partie du manuscrit se lit à la fin du premier quaternion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
